@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #486777
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #EEF5FA
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #486777
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #F7FAFC
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF3DA
skinparam noteBorderColor #B59865
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45
title Trust boundaries and candidate threats
top to bottom direction
rectangle "TB1 — Untrusted entry\nBrowser / Git client / uploaded content" as entry #FFF3DA
rectangle "TB2 — Product authority boundary\nExact identity / resource / action / current state\nContent validation is separate from permission" as product
database "Protected information\nPrivate records / actual history\nRepository context / scoped credentials" as data
rectangle "TB3 — Provider boundary\nSelected Google account and operation\nReconcile uncertain remote effects" as provider
rectangle "TB4 — Conditional code boundary\nUntrusted code / YAML / outputs\nIsolation and resource evidence required" as run #FFF3DA
rectangle "TB5 — Operator / recovery boundary\nRestricted evidence / current authority\nRestored access and external-state checks" as ops
entry --> product : SQ-T01/02: wrong or stale authority\nSQ-T03: unsafe supplied content
product --> data : SQ-T07: reference/usage race\nSQ-T08: stale revision context
product --> provider : SQ-T05/06: wrong account / duplicate effect
product --> run : SQ-T04: excessive host/secret/target powers
run --> ops : SQ-T09: sensitive output disclosure
data --> ops : SQ-T10: restored old rights/effects
note bottom of ops
SQ-T11: a healthy page or missing alert is not assurance.
SQ-T12: competing workloads can exhaust shared resources.
These cross-cutting cases affect all applicable boundaries.
end note

legend bottom
Arrows identify selected information/power crossings and candidate threats, not proven exploits.
Boundary labels state required controls; configuration and effectiveness have not been verified.
endlegend
@enduml
